            "review_title": "Review at Danang Food Center",
            "review_text": "Daisy E\nLondon, United Kingdom3 contributions\n0\nWorst meal in Vietnam\nAug 2019 • Family\nWe ate here as a family on a Saturday night while waiting for the dragon bridge to breathe fire. There was hardly anyone eating in, only us three and one other table. Despite the fact there were more staff than customers, the service was slow and poor. Finished plates and glasses were not cleared, even with staff stood around the table. Several items on the menu were unavailable even though it was still early. I ordered the crispy squid and asked if it came with rice. I was told yes, but when it arrived it was simply chunks of dry squid on its own- no rice as promised, no salad or anything. Additionally, a stage and microphone were being set up as we ate. Throughout our entire meal, one of the workers found it hilarious to shout and hiss down the microphone, completely over the top, and this between bursts of feedback made the atmosphere unbearable. At one point, he shouted down the microphone so loudly it made all staff and customers jump and physically hurt the ears. Only this prompted the ‘manager’ to go and speak to them, which made no difference as they carried on as before. 3 conversations from the manager later and it was no better. Food quality was okay but compared to the standard of Vietnamese cuisine in Da Nang and Hoi An this restaurant was disappointing. Steer clear!\nRead more\nWritten September 2, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
